NetBird artwork
===============

The NetBird mark used by this widget comes from the NetBird client, unmodified:

    https://github.com/netbirdio/netbird
    commit 11733fd718fb7889cfbf8b4e6498c0b4e74a1eb0 (2026-08-28)

(c) 2022 NetBird GmbH & AUTHORS, licensed BSD-3-Clause. The upstream repository
places management/, signal/, relay/ and combined/ under AGPLv3; client/ui/ is
not among them, so this artwork is BSD-3-Clause.

Vector geometry (default "theme" style)
---------------------------------------

The two wing paths in NetbirdIcon.qml are copied verbatim from

    client/ui/frontend/src/assets/logos/netbird.svg
    sha256 64773bd313506a921e51558fdb0c243da6fb0c0df0a81c1f2cd4bc733a54838e

so the widget can draw the mark in the current theme's colours at any size.
That file carries three paths; the third fills the overlap between the two
wings in a second colour, which changes nothing once every path is drawn in one
colour, so it is not reproduced. The same geometry appears upstream at
client/ui/assets/svg/netbird-menu.svg and proxy/web/src/assets/netbird.svg.

The state badges (check, dots, cross) are drawn by this widget rather than
copied; they mirror the badges on the tray PNGs below.

Bitmaps (opt-in "color" style)
------------------------------

From client/ui/assets/, used as-is:

    netbird-systemtray-<state>.png   256x256

for <state> in connected, connecting, disconnected, error, needs-login. At this
commit netbird-systemtray-needs-login.png is byte-identical to
netbird-systemtray-error.png; both names ship so the widget's state-to-file
mapping stays a plain lookup.

